<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF, Siemens merge units.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF, Siemens merge units.</headline>
<dateline>LE BOURGET, France 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French electronics company Thomson-CSF and Siemens of Germany said on Tuesday they are putting their air traffic management activities into a joint venture.</p>
<p>The new company, called Airsys ATM, will be 60 percent owned by Thomson-CSF Airsys and 40 percent by Siemens AG. It will have revenues of 2.2 billion francs ($376.8 million) and employ 1,600 people, the companies said in a statement at the Paris air show. ($ = 5.839 French Francs)</p>
</text>
